{"cuisine/lakota-foodways":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/lakota-foodways","n":"Lakota foodways","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Indigenous foodways, Northern Plains, South Dakota and North Dakota","names":"Lakota","intro":[["Lakota life on the Northern Plains centers on ",["Bison","ingredient/bison"],", tatanka, a sacred animal that gives food, clothing, shelter and tools. Meat is dried in thin strips, and dried meat mixed with fat and chokecherries becomes wasna, the Lakota form of ",["Pemmican","dish/pemmican"],", made to last through hard winters. Corn came by trade with the Mandan villages."],["Wild berries, traditionally chokecherries, are cooked into ",["Wojapi","dish/wojapi"],", eaten with ",["Frybread","dish/frybread"]," or alongside meat. Today bison are returning to tribal lands, and Oglala Lakota chef Sean Sherman cooks with Indigenous foods only, leaving out wheat flour, dairy and cane sugar."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"North Dakota Studies, The Lakota bison hunt","url":"https://www.ndstudies.gov/gr8/node/261"},{"name":"Black Hills and Badlands Tourism, The flavor of culture","url":"https://www.blackhillsbadlands.com/blog/post/the-flavor-of-culture-indigenous-cuisine-in-the-black-hills-badlands/"},{"name":"Partnership With Native Americans, Wojapi","url":"https://nativepartnership.org/wojapi-recipe/"},{"name":"MPR News, The Sioux Chef uses only Native ingredients","url":"https://www.mprnews.org/story/2022/10/24/the-sioux-chef-uses-only-native-ingredients-but-isnt-cooking-like-its-1491"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"lakota-foodways"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Frybread","dish/frybread"],["Pemmican","dish/pemmican"],["Wojapi","dish/wojapi"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Owamni","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"owamni.com","note":"Sean Sherman's Minneapolis restaurant, cooking only with Indigenous 