de with durum wheat, macaroni is commonly cut in short lengths; curved macaroni may be referred to as \"elbow macaroni\". Some home machines can make macaroni shapes but, like most pasta, macaroni is usually made commercially by large-scale extrusion. The common curved shape is created by different speeds of extrusion on opposite sides of the pasta tube as it comes out of the machine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-macaroni"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroni"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Johnny Marzetti","dish/johnny-marzetti"],["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"]]],["Canadian cuisine","cuisine/canadian-cuisine",[["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"]]],["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine",[["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ground beef","ingredient/ground-beef"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cheddar cheese","ingredient/cheddar-cheese"],["Cheddar sauce","ingredient/cheddar-sauce"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/01/Macaroni2.jpg/500px-Macaroni2.jpg","w":500,"h":328,"by":"Popo le Chien","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Macaroni2.jpg"}},"ingredient/prunus-dulcis":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/prunus-dulcis","n":"Prunus dulcis","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The almond (Prunus amygdalus, syn. Prunus dulcis (Mill.) D.A.Webb, nom. illeg. non Prunus dulcis Rouchy) is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-prunus-dulcis"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_dulcis"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine",[["Kransekage","dish/kransekage"]]],["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine",[["Kransekage","dish/kransekage"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/500px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ivar Leidus","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg"}},"dish/ossetian-pie":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ossetian-pie","n":"Ossetian pie","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Ossetian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ossetian cuisine refers to the cooking styles and dishes of the Ossetians of the Caucasus."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ossetian-pie"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ossetian_pie"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Ossetian cuisine","cuisine/ossetian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Ossetian cuisine","links":[["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Ossetian cheese","dish/ossetian-cheese"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6c/Ossetian_pirogi_are_put_in_the_center_of_festive_table.jpg/500px-Ossetian_pirogi_are_put_in_the_center_of_festive_table.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Геор сотник","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ossetian_pirogi_are_put_in_the_center_of_festive_table.jpg"}},"ingredient/anchovies-as-food":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/anchovies-as-food","n":"Anchovies as food","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 5 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Anchovies are small, common saltwater forage fish in the family Engraulidae that are used as human food and fish bait.  There are 144 species in 17 genera found in the Atlantic, Indian, and Pacific Oceans. Anchovies are usually classified as oily fish. They are small, green fish with blue reflections due to a silver longitudinal stripe that runs from the base of the caudal fin.  They range from 2 centimetres (0.79 in) to 40 centimetres (16 in) in adult length, and the body shape is variable, with more slender fish in northern populations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-anchovies-as-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchovies_as_food"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Rempeyek","dish/rempeyek"],["Sambal","dish/sambal"],["Sambal tuktuk","dish/sambal-tuktuk"]]],["Basilicatan (Lucanian) cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-basilicata",[["Tumact me tulez","dish/tumact-me-tulez"]]],["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Pasta con le sarde","dish/pasta-con-le-sarde"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Breadcrumbs","ingredient/breadcrumbs"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Chilli pepper","ingredient/chilli-pepper"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["European pilchard","ingredient/european-pilchard"],["Fennel","ingredient/fennel"],["Pine nut","ingredient/pine-nut"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Saffron","ingredient/saffron"],["Sardines as food","ingredient/sardines-as-food"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Peanut","ingredient/peanut"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img